--------------------------------------------------------------
|NOT IN|

Find employees whose department isn't in the departments table.

SELECT *
FROM employees
WHERE department NOT IN (
    SELECT department_name
    FROM departments
);

There's an important NULL behavior with NOT IN that can cause surprising results in real SQL. For production queries, NOT EXISTS is often safer when NULLs are possible.

